<title>USA: PNC Bank unit to sell Home Mortgage stake.</title>
<headline>PNC Bank unit to sell Home Mortgage stake.</headline>
<dateline>VERNON HILLS, Ill. 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>PNC Mortgage, a unit of PNC Bank Corp, said Friday it will sell its 50-percent stake in the Home Mortgage Network to HFS Inc for an undisclosed price.</p>
<p>Home Mortgage Network is an Illinois-based joint venture between Pittsburgh-based PNC Mortgage and HFS, which is based in Parsippany, N.J. It was created in 1995 to provide neutral, multi-lender mortgage origination services from Coldwell Banker officers, the companies said.</p>
<p>HFS became a 50-percent owner of Home Mortgage Network with its acquisition of Coldwell Banker in 1996.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
</text>
